# M7's done-when on QEMU with the selftest kernel (user/root/src/console.rs;
# docs/design.md, "Scenarios" under "User-level drivers and console"): two
# clients write interleaved lines through console, and input typed by the
# harness reaches the right client. The root task starts watch (255), which
# receives the servers' faults, uart (200), which drives COM1 through an
# IOPort capability and IRQ 4 (an edge pin: wait, Ack, service), and
# console (150), each server in a CSpace and VSpace of its own built from
# the root task's image frames. It attaches as client 1 and points print!
# at console, then drives clients a (badge 2) and b (badge 3), at 100, one
# step at a time through their Calls on endpoint D, so every write boundary
# is fixed. Each piece below is distinct, so a piece console put inside
# another line would be missing from its own: console keeps each client's
# unfinished line until its newline. The 300-byte b2 line arrives in three
# 100-byte writes with a's whole line between them; b's burst of twelve
# 200-byte lines makes uart hold some of console's writes. Then each client
# writes a prompt and reads; the harness focuses b with Ctrl-T 3 and types
# its line, then focuses a and types a line with a typo, DEL and Ctrl-U.
# Root checks each client read exactly its line, and uart's Stats: receive
# and THRE interrupts served, exactly the 22 bytes sent, no overruns. The
# echoed input lines are not expected: whether a prompt shows depends on
# whether the client's Read came before its input (host tests pin echo).
cmdline: test=console
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: cmdline: "test=console"
expect: root: microL4 root task
expect: root: cmdline "test=console"
expect: console: watch (TCB slot
expect: priority 255) receives the servers' faults; uart (TCB slot
expect: priority 200) holds copies of the COM1 IOPort
expect: GSI 4, edge, active high); console (TCB slot
expect: priority 150); each server in a CSpace and VSpace of its own
expect: console: root is client 1; its output goes through console from here
expect: console: clients a (badge 2) and b (badge 3), priority 100
expect: a1 alpha one
expect: b1 bravo one
expect: a2 short
expect: b2 0123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901 end
expect: a3 x
expect: a4 y
expect: b3 z
expect: a5 end
expect: console: interleaved lines written, in 11 steps
expect: b burst 01 abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabc 01
expect: b burst 02 abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabc 02
